IMPORT prelude

-- Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 (Qld) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- Built-in date functions only (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR), not the
-- daydate library. The Act counts in days ("within 28 days of receiving", ss 141(1), 142(2), 166(1), 167(4)(c), 168(2),
-- 168A(3)(d), 169(2), (3), 170(2)), in a year ("within 1 year of the alleged contravention", ss 138(1), 175(1)) and in
-- months ("6 months after informing", s 167(1)).
--
-- Unofficial version. Based on content from the Queensland Legislation website at 6 November 2026. (c) The State of
-- Queensland, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Anti-Discrimination Act 1991`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

-- "within N days of" or "after" a day: the day itself is not counted, so the last day is that day plus N (fork F1).
GIVEN `the number of days` IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `the number of days` `days after` `the start` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS `the number of days`)

GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE, `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` `the first` `is on or before` `the second` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the first` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `the second`

GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE, `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of` `the first` `and` `the second` MEANS
    IF `the day` `the first` `is on or before` `the second`
    THEN `the second`
    ELSE `the first`

-- A Gregorian leap year.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `leap year` y IF
        (y MODULO 4 EQUALS 0)
    AND (    (NOT (y MODULO 100 EQUALS 0))
         OR  (y MODULO 400 EQUALS 0))

-- The number of days in a month of a year.
GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in month` m `of` y MEANS
    BRANCH IF m EQUALS 2 THEN (IF `leap year` y THEN 29 ELSE 28)
           IF m EQUALS 4 THEN 30
           IF m EQUALS 6 THEN 30
           IF m EQUALS 9 THEN 30
           IF m EQUALS 11 THEN 30
           OTHERWISE 31

-- The same day of the same month a number of whole years on; 29 February in a year that has none is 28 February
-- (fork F2).
GIVEN `the years` IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` `the years` `years after` `the start` MEANS
    IF     (DATE_DAY `the start` EQUALS 29)
       AND (DATE_MONTH `the start` EQUALS 2)
       AND (NOT (`leap year` (DATE_YEAR `the start` PLUS `the years`)))
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 (DATE_YEAR `the start` PLUS `the years`)
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY (DATE_DAY `the start`) (DATE_MONTH `the start`) (DATE_YEAR `the start` PLUS `the years`)

-- The same day of the month a number of whole months on; where that month is shorter, its last day (fork F2).
GIVEN `the months` IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the same day` `the months` `months after` `the start` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY `the day of the month` `the new month` `the new year`
    WHERE
        `the month index` MEANS (DATE_MONTH `the start` MINUS 1) PLUS `the months`
        `the new month` MEANS (`the month index` MODULO 12) PLUS 1
        `the new year` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the start` PLUS ((`the month index` MINUS (`the month index` MODULO 12)) DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the day of the month` MEANS
            IF DATE_DAY `the start` GREATER THAN (`the days in month` `the new month` `of` `the new year`)
            THEN `the days in month` `the new month` `of` `the new year`
            ELSE DATE_DAY `the start`
